WEBVTT

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.400
Yeah, it's currently in production.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:07.730
How are things proceeding on your end?

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.130
Reporting in!

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:13.610
I've currently got great surveillance on the 
Azure Brigade's main base, Uranus Castle.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.620
Marquis Conrad just left for the 
imperial capital moments ago.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.010
Looks like he's hoping to petition for 
an opportunity to rejoin the empire.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.780
<i>Well, not much we can do there.</i>

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.760
<i>So what about the you-know-what?</i>

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.520
I've found it!

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:28.130
<i>I see.</i>

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.840
<i>In that case, make sure you're out of there
before matters are set in motion.</i>

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.560
Roger that.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.410
<i>With the Azure Brigade reforging 
ties with the empire,</i>

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.010
<i>it's dangerous to be here.</i>

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.590
<i>However...</i>

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.420
<b>High School Prodigies Have It Easy
Even In Another World!</b>

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:19.320
<b>It Seems Keine
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hCan't Stand Naughty Boys!</b>

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:29.240
Is this... an epidemic?

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.320
Miasma enters through the wounds 
and eventually causes death.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.260
Keine called it septicemia.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.990
Doctor, please save my daughter!

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:42.430
Unfortunately... we're out of holy water.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:43.910
That can't be!

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.300
Holy water?

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:50.330
It's a medicine Keine created 
that she calls antibiotics.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.940
We've had so many patients 
that production can't keep up.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.720
Mama, where are you?

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:57.610
I'm here!

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:58.890
I'm right here!

00:02:58.890 --> 00:02:59.980
It hurts.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.280
It hurts.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.570
Akatsuki!

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.660
Please, save my Melinda!

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.340
Please!

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:13.020
<i>I don't have the power 
to save these people...</i>

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.300
What a cold-hearted god!

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.750
Forsaking an ailing child.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.520
This is practically a sight out of hell.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.770
I see the god of the Seven-Light Faith

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.310
has no intention of saving the people
 who suffer from this plague.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.300
Who are those people?

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.810
Members of the Medical Guild in Gustave.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.080
Indeed.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.820
I am the head of the 
Medical Guild, Serentius.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.760
Would you like us to save her for you?

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:41.780
Huh?!

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.960
If you use this secret medicine,

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:47.030
you'll be able to relieve 
your child of their pain.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.370
Count Serentius, that's...

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.600
P-Please!

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.630
Please save my child!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.130
As if!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.350
I do apologize!

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:02.380
The use of our secret medicine, opium,

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.640
has been forbidden by the 
Seven-Light Faith's angel, Keine!

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.210
How could you...

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:10.300
If you must,

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:15.150
then resent the Seven-Light Faith,
 which leaves the ill to suffer.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.680
You bastards!

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.400
Lowly humans.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.900
Who ever said that we 
would not save this child?

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.420
We will save her indeed!

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:29.370
We will save this girl, and all 
of the other patients as well,

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:35.120
through the miracle of the healing power 
that I have bestowed upon my angel, Keine!

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.380
Huh?

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.000
Precisely, Akatsuki.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.010
Keine!

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.630
Save them?

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.040
How?

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.260
You're out of your holy water, aren't you?

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.540
You're right.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:56.970
We can't supply the necessary amount of 
penicillin, or what you call holy water.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:01.930
Which is why I'll be making 
medicine with this.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.690
That's... coal?

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.120
You're going to make medicine from a rock?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.620
This is terrific!

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.000
That's an angel for you!

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.560
Very well.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:21.000
However, if your medicine fails to treat it,

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.130
then you'll have to lift 
your ban on our opium!

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.510
Yes, that won't be a problem.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.480
Th-Thank you so much, angel!

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:43.480
No, I've only soothed her pain.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:47.230
People don't accept death that easily.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:50.490
So please don't give up and 
continue to encourage Melinda.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.200
Yes!

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:54.970
I'm sorry.

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:59.000
He was ticking me off,
so I went and ran my mouth.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.640
No, you did well.

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.880
That's our God, Akatsuki!

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:10.390
Can you really create 
medicine from coal, though?

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.040
Of course.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:15.210
You can make the miracle drug 
that once defeated septicemia,

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.280
the "magic bullet."

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:25.580
We're going to make the medicine ourselves?

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:29.030
Isn't it better to ask Ringo 
to handle something like this?

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:30.380
It is.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:34.840
However, she's currently spending 
all of her time on that one project.

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.570
Sorry for the wait!

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.700
Lyrule?

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:45.000
I was planning to borrow 
Lyrule's magic power for this.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.170
Her magic?

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.440
Yes.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.590
After some discussion with 
Tsukasa and Ringo,

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:54.640
we've concluded that magic in 
this world is a technology

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.520
that acts upon substances 
at the atomic level.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.770
In which case, controlling the 
chemical reactions of substances,

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.520
or the manufacture of medicines, 
should be possible.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.520
If my magic can help, then I'll do it!

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.750
Well, let's get started, then.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:14.120
First, we steam the coal, and separate 
out the coke and the coal tar.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:15.280
Yes!

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.950
There's something black and syrupy...

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:27.210
That's good.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:32.430
Now heat up that coal tar and transfer 
the steam from it to that pot there.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.580
Yes!

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.010
Well done.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.350
That's benzene.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:38.720
It's pretty.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.230
You'll die if you breathe in too 
much of it, so please be careful.

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.310
I'll die?!

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.780
Is this really gonna work?

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.320
I have no idea.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:52.200
Next, we're going to use this sulfuric acid.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.280
You'll melt to death if you touch it,
so make certain you don't.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.530
I'll <i>melt</i> and die?!

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.540
Next we add in this ammonia water.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:07.290
This smells like pee.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:12.050
Yes, because it is like 
incredibly condensed pee.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:15.760
I-I am making medicine, aren't I?!

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.220
Yes, of course you are.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:32.740
It's finished.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:34.740
So that powder's the medicine?

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.030
Yes,

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:39.240
this is human history's first 
synthesized antimicrobial,

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.660
the magic bullet, sulfonamide.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:48.750
Now, everyone, administer 
this sulfonamide to every patient.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.130
Yes!

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.780
Mama?

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.610
Melinda?!

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:15.630
Temperature, pulse, and breathing all stable.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.110
She'll be fine now.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.140
Angel!

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.450
Thank you so very much!

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:26.240
No, you're the one who saved Melinda.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:27.080
Huh?

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:31.460
Sulfonamide only stops 
the growth of pathogens.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:36.410
It was Melinda's own vitality that 
defeated the pathogens within her.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:39.530
This girl was able to keep fighting them off

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:42.220
thanks to you encouraging her as her mother.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.730
You both won this battle.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.860
What a naughty boy.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:03.200
To think she'd honestly 
create medicine from a rock!

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.140
At this rate, we'll be out of business!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.830
What do we do, Count?!

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:12.350
That medicine was made by 
their mage woman, wasn't it?

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:14.170
That's what I hear.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:18.340
Then threaten that girl and get her 
to change the medicine into poison.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.890
I don't care if you have to torture her.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:23.770
Once patients start dying from
the Seven-Light Faith's medicine,

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:26.660
their power and reputation will be gone.

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:31.360
I knew you all would come 
to an idea like that.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.780
Good evening, Count Serentius.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:37.240
Wh-Why are you here?!

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.460
Please don't be so wary of me.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:42.740
I've only come here to persuade you.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:48.040
M-My body won't move?!

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.720
What are you planning to do?!

00:10:58.440 --> 00:10:59.960
I told you, didn't I?

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:02.310
I'm only here to persuade you.

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:05.470
Directly through your brain.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:10.360
Did you know it's possible 
to change a person's

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:13.280
opinions, personality, and everything 
else to suit your needs?

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:16.570
It's easy when you tinker with their brain.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.480
A-All right!

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:20.240
I'll give up on the opium!

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.950
I'll serve you for the rest of my life!

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:24.270
Just please spare me!

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.120
Don't be so frightened.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:28.630
The anesthesia will kick in soon.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:31.460
D-Demon!

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:38.250
That's right.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:42.260
That label suits me far better than angel.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:48.010
To be honest, I despise God so much,
I wish I could kill him.

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:50.780
As a doctor, I've openly thought,

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:55.600
"If God had only created mankind with 
proper, healthy minds and bodies,

00:11:55.600 --> 00:12:00.030
then mankind would never have to 
suffer from diseases or wars."

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:02.560
I find it unforgivable

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:08.900
that our incompetent creator would make
such endearing beings with so many flaws!

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:14.290
So I intend to correct 
all of his ineptitude.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:19.070
I will grant these weak bodies 
destined for death an eternal life.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:24.300
I will patch those weak minds that dare 
to hurt others into perfect minds.

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:29.720
And in doing so, I will create a world

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:33.210
where all are free of flaws and deficiencies.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.830
Thank you!

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:41.070
I'm truly glad you're doing better!

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:45.050
A patient's smile is the greatest
medal of honor, Lady Keine!

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:46.750
Yes, it is.

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:47.770
Yes!

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:52.190
Our Medical Guild will support the 
Seven-Light Faith with all our power!

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:54.460
Now, off to work, off to work!

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:59.680
I heard his values had changed after he 
was attacked by robbers in his mansion,

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.680
but he feels like a completely different 
person, and it's kind of creepy.

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:04.590
Try to get along with him, though.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:07.970
He's a very good boy now.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.990
It's been a long time, Conrad.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:30.990
I'm truly grateful that you've made time in 
your busy schedule to see me, General Neuro!

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.150
Don't be so tense.

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:37.580
I have no intention of 
chastising the Azure Brigade.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:42.440
While I acknowledged Gustave's 
loyalty to His Majesty,

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:45.150
there are limits to everything.

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:48.600
Allowing one's domain to starve and 
grow frail is out of the question.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:52.380
The Azure Brigade simply killed 
and consumed the weak Gustave.

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:56.400
That's well within the empire's 
policy of survival of the fittest.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.770
It's commendable, even.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:01.150
Th-Then you mean we—

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:06.110
However, the Seven Light-Faith... 
They are unacceptable.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:10.730
That reminds me. I hear the Azure Brigade 
is working with the Seven-Light Faith.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.620
That's...

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.920
I jest.

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:17.050
Your Azure Brigade

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:21.000
currently lacks the forces to fight 
against the Seven-Light Faith, right?

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.810
Y-Yes!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:26.210
So we shall supplement your forces.

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:35.690
This is my adjutant, Tanganika.

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:38.270
Show him your power.

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:42.810
That's...

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:48.740
That's just like L'age Soleil?

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:52.240
It is a bona-fide L'age Soleil.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:57.450
H-He can manifest L'age Soleil, 
that grand magic, in an instant?

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:02.830
I'll lend this exceptional mage to 
the Azure Brigade to support you.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:06.440
I'll even send 10,000 troops 
as reinforcements.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:08.430
With those forces on your side,

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:12.760
you won't need to bow down to the 
Seven-Light Faith any longer, will you?

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.000
Yes!

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:18.310
We shall surely eliminate those 
impudent fools defying the empire!

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:24.320
Only one man is fit to stand above 
the people in all the lands,

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.900
His Imperial Majesty Lindworm.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:33.240
The Seven-Light Faith, which proclaims 
false gods and preaches equality for all

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.660
will not be tolerated.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:39.310
Looks like you finished it.

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:41.120
Thank you, Ringo.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.420
Yeah. Though...

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:48.560
was it really a good idea to bring 
one of these into this world?

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:49.870
Ringo.

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:53.670
What do you think it 
takes to create a nation?

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:56.640
I don't know.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.220
Nothing.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.360
Huh?

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:02.460
For example, say some 
children build a secret base

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:05.340
and declare that base to be their own nation.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:09.080
In that very moment, we witness the 
birth of a nation of children.

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:10.860
R-Really?

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:15.040
Naturally, though, the adults around them
won't stand for it.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:16.370
They'll destroy the secret base,

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:20.870
scold the children, and the nation 
of children will collapse.

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:24.940
It's very easy to found a nation,

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:28.540
but it takes power to 
maintain its sovereignty.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:34.470
<i>Count Blumhardt,</i>

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:39.560
<i>I will make sure the Azure Brigade 
you created changes the empire...</i>

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:43.130
<i>into a nation where people 
can live more humanely.</i>

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.280
Raisenach?

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.940
I thought you headed out to help 
rebuild the impoverished villages?

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:52.690
Oh, I finished that up sooner than expected.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.610
Then where's Count Conrad?

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:57.130
He headed straight to his meeting.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:17:00.370
Are you sure you shouldn't 
be with him as his guard?

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:04.370
Yeah, we were given other orders.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.590
You dodged it? What a pain.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.050
What do you think you're doing?!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.280
I told you. Following orders.

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:16.880
To kill you.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:18.430
Why me?!

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.570
Don't any of you interfere.

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:22.430
I'll put her down myself.

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.850
Do you really think that's going to work?!

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.120
Shoot her!

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:50.710
This is cowardly, Raisenach!

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.360
Shut up.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:55.720
Have you no pride as a knight?!

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:02.280
Both lord and retainer are so naive!

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:06.090
Blumhardt said the exact 
same thing as he died.

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:08.830
Have I no pride as a knight? Hah!

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.980
What do you mean?

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.910
You're dense.

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:17.440
I'm telling you that I'm the 
one who killed Blumhardt.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:18.340
Wha?!

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:22.030
Though, really, Gustave went too far.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.740
If you kill off the peasants,

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:26.600
then who are we supposed 
to wring taxes out of?

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:29.500
You scumbag!

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.540
It'd be a waste to just kill her.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.200
Yeah, have at her.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.720
Man, this is exciting.

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.920
Make some nice screams for us, too.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.060
Stop!

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:54.260
What?

00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:59.820
Looks like I made it in the nick of time!

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.450
Yoohoo!

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.050
Been a while, Jeanne!

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.240
Shinobu?!

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:08.450
This looks like a purge of
the doves in the Azure Brigade.

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:11.580
The Azure Brigade has decided 
to rejoin the empire

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:14.600
and fight the Seven-Light Faith, right?

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:16.460
Troublesome woman.

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:19.050
Shinobu, why?

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:20.470
Because we're friends.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.120
Let's go, Jeanne.

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:23.500
Yes!

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:26.990
Little shits.

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:29.480
One extra person won't make any difference!

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:36.940
Jeanne!

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.590
That sword...

00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:57.020
Yes.

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:59.590
It was Count Blumhardt's sword.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:03.590
I asked to have it as a memento
 after the last battle.

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.600
You really looked up to the Count, huh?

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:12.600
I'm the woman I am today 
because of Count Blumhardt.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:17.610
There's something I want you to see, Jeanne.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:24.320
I can't believe there was a place 
like this beneath Uranus Castle.

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:27.120
It's an underground shelter 
only a few people know about.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:30.620
It's the perfect place to hide secrets.

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:32.620
Secrets?

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:34.250
Is that...

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:39.630
the golden statue?

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:45.640
Count Conrad said he didn't know where 
it went, but he took it in secret.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:50.760
The golden statue built from taxing the 
people until they were skin and bones...

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:52.890
He stole it?!

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:57.080
Count Blumhardt...

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:00.390
said the current empire was wrong.

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:04.220
He said survival of the fittest 
may be a law of nature,

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:07.220
but that makes us no different than animals.

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:13.480
He said that people should aid and 
support each other to live nobly.

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:19.420
The Azure Brigade was founded 
upon those ideals, so this...

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:22.550
The Azure Brigade may have changed,

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:25.900
but those ideals still 
remain as vividly as ever.

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:27.800
Deep within your heart.

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:31.620
Come with me.

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:37.000
The Seven-Light Faith will accept those 
sentiments you and the Count shared.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:45.530
For the ideals of Count Blumhardt 
that dwell within this sword,

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:48.450
and for my own sake as well,

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:51.450
I shall accompany you.

00:21:52.150 --> 00:21:53.000
Yeah!

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:56.960
Hide!

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:02.540
<i>That's Count Conrad.</i>

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:03.960
<i>Also...</i>

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:09.190
<i>That can't be!</i>
